the future being assembled piece by  piece at unlv a human-like robot  developed by engineer students  attracting worldwide attention in fact  the team just advanced in a global  competition and was selected as one of  15 across the world to compete next fall  10 million dollars on the line but the  technology being created right here is  priceless  meet avatar hubo standing five feet five  inches tall weighing in at 175 pounds  this robot looks every bit the part of a  hollywood movie but here inside the  robotics lab at unlv the real stars are  the ones who've dedicated gears to this  groundbreaking technology so many late  nights in this lab so many days so many  weekends there's always improvements dr  gene chagus vass is the team captain and  lead engineer my ultimate goal is to  have let's say a firefighter that can  embody the robot and perform the same  job but at a safe location it's all  possible with this special haptic suit  i'm able to feel whatever  touch is applied to the robot be that a  light touch or something with force it  varies with the amount of pressure that  you decide to put onto the robot and the  special virtual reality headset allows  the wearer to see what hubo sees because  it uses two cameras it  creates stereographic vision much like  our eyes work that helps with depth  perception which allows for more  lifelike movement it's just tracking the  motion of the arm and then sending that  data over to the actual arm of the robot  there's no joystick there are no cables  avatar hubo is unlimited in its movement  dr chagas vas says the implications for  this kind of technology are endless as  for the immediate future his team will  focus on developing hubos fine motor  skills manipulate and move at the same  time that's a very complicated task for  robot even though you can hug and high  five hubo and share emotion through the  avatar screen  don't worry robots aren't taking over  the world  yet no we're not trying to make the  robots conquer the world but rather  we're trying to you know improve the way  of life  the team says one of the things that  they're going to accomplish for the  global competition is walking and  holding hands with avatar hubo
 

